\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Which parameters survive coarse-graining}
\date{2026-11-28}

\p{Averaging adjacent pairs on a path can couple the two end blocks,
even when their original vertices are not neighbors
(\ref{fdip-0099}). Averaging nested residue classes instead preserves
the hierarchical form (\ref{fdip-009A}). Both operations discard
coordinates, but their effects on the retained precision differ.}

\p{For an orthogonal projection, the retained field and the discarded
fluctuation occupy perpendicular subspaces. Is that geometric separation
enough to make their Gaussian probabilities independent, or must the
precision preserve the separation as well?}
